# SPIDER's kits (drumline.h DL_KITS; smk37.c lsmk_kit_put): a new project's kit is ACOUSTIC (its keys samples: SLOOP's
# acoustic kit, in SPIDER's bank); SEL's list on the kit's Engine page offers KIT first (the kit it has): ALGORITHM picks
# one, SEL puts it on (the eleven keys, the track's name). A key changed: a kit of its own, KIT offers ACOUSTIC. The drum
# pads play whichever kit is on (pad 16: ACOUSTIC's crash)
wait 300
expect trk 1
expect kit 1
expect par1.d1.model 10
expect par1.d8.model 10
expect par1.d3.mode 3
shot kit_acoustic.png
# 909: its samples on kick, snare, hat and clap, the models on the rest
tap EDIT
expect page Engine
tap SEL
shot kit_list.png
turn ALGO 1 30
tap SEL
expect kit 2
expect par1.d1.model 10
expect par1.d1.k1 0
expect par1.d4.model 2
# SYNTH: LOOM-8's own kit, every key a model
tap SEL
turn ALGO 1 30
tap SEL
expect kit 3
expect par1.d1.model 0
expect par1.d11.model 9
# a key changed: no kit of the three; KIT offers ACOUSTIC, SEL puts it back
param 1 d1.volume 70
expect kit 0
tap SEL
tap SEL
expect kit 1
expect par1.d1.volume 87
# the drum pads: ACOUSTIC's crash on pad 16, whatever track is selected
spin ALGO 1
expect trk 2
expect drumhits 0
tappad 15 100
expect drumhits 1
wait 200
shot kit_crash.png
